{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "phi(18446744073709551615) = 9208981628670443520\n  how: 18446744073709551615 = 3 * 5 * 17 * 257 * 641 * 65537 * 6700417; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2 * 4 * 16 * 256 * 640 * 65536 * 6700416\n  the order of the unit group (Z/18446744073709551615)*; lambda(18446744073709551615) = 17153064960 is its exponent\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "phi", "ucas": "phi 18446744073709551615", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "phi", "method": "18446744073709551615 = 3 * 5 * 17 * 257 * 641 * 65537 * 6700417; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2 * 4 * 16 * 256 * 640 * 65536 * 6700416", "lhs": "phi(18446744073709551615)", "value": "9208981628670443520", "headline": "phi(18446744073709551615) = 9208981628670443520", "details": ["the order of the unit group (Z/18446744073709551615)*; lambda(18446744073709551615) = 17153064960 is its exponent"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "phi(18446744073709551615) = 9208981628670443520\n  how: 18446744073709551615 = 3 * 5 * 17 * 257 * 641 * 65537 * 6700417; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2 * 4 * 16 * 256 * 640 * 65536 * 6700416\n  the order of the unit group (Z/18446744073709551615)*; lambda(18446744073709551615) = 17153064960 is its exponent\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "3825123056546413051 = 149491 * 747451 * 34233211 (not prime)\n  a Carmichael number: a^(n-1) = 1 for every a coprime to it (lambda(3825123056546413051) = 171166050 divides n - 1), so Fermat's test is fooled\n  how: trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)\n  check: the product is 3825123056546413051; each factor is prime\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "factorint", "ucas": "factorint 3825123056546413051", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factorint", "a_carmichael_number": "a^(n-1) = 1 for every a coprime to it (lambda(3825123056546413051) = 171166050 divides n - 1), so Fermat's test is fooled", "method": "trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)", "lhs": "3825123056546413051", "annotation": "not prime", "value": "149491 * 747451 * 34233211", "headline": "3825123056546413051 = 149491 * 747451 * 34233211 (not prime)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the product is 3825123056546413051; each factor is prime"}], "files": [], "text": "3825123056546413051 = 149491 * 747451 * 34233211 (not prime)\n  a Carmichael number: a^(n-1) = 1 for every a coprime to it (lambda(3825123056546413051) = 171166050 divides n - 1), so Fermat's test is fooled\n  how: trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)\n  check: the product is 3825123056546413051; each factor is prime\n"}, "isError": false}}
